# OpenSIPS' codec-stripping path trimmed trailing spaces off the last
# SDP payload by walking a pointer backwards off the start of the
# parsed value, so a crafted codec parameter whose value was all
# spaces (or empty) read whatever preceded the buffer (out-of-bounds
# read, CWE-125; GHSA-3ghx-j39m-cw4f, Enable Security's 2021/2022
# audit). stream_process in modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c already had
# the bounded spelling eight lines above --
# `while (found.s > lmp->u.value && *(found.s - 1) == ' ')` -- and
# then, under `if (cur == lmp->u.value + lmp->len)`, walked
# `tmp = found.s; while (*(--tmp) == ' ')` with no floor at all: the
# pre-decrement runs and dereferences before anything compares the
# cursor against the base it came from. The fixing commit dd051f8ed5
# ("[sipmsgops] fix codec_delete_XX() parsing", one line) bounds it:
# `while (tmp>lmp->u.value && *(--tmp) == ' ')`. No pool correction.
#
# ## What fires, both revisions
#
# Three --cache off runs per revision over modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c
# report **20 findings each, deterministically, identically on the
# vulnerable parent a1406ad8 and the fixed dd051f8ed5**: 10 VYQL-MEM-010,
# 7 VYQL-MEM-016 RawMemoryCopySize (codecs.c:138/221/579/582/621/637/658),
# 2 VYQL-MEM-006 NullableDeref (codecs.c:369 and 570) and 1 VYQL-MEM-020
# (codecs.c:386), byte-identical by rule and line. The full findings view
# was read, not the `-flags` only view. **Nothing sits on line 562**, the
# loop that
# is the defect: the scanner reports the guarded memcpy sizes and the
# forward-shift deref at 570, and nothing about the unbounded walk --
# the "findings in the function are not coverage" shape, twice
# independently recorded on mbedtls. A minimal repro holding only the
# guarded unbounded walk reports **0 findings**. The 1st pass's zero
# was real.
#
# ## Why nothing ships
#
# `vyql graph` on the repro shows the loop condition never enters the
# IR at all: c.go's `case "while_statement", "for_statement",
# "do_statement"` (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go:1075)
# lowers `nir.Loop{Body: c.collectBlocks(n)}` and drops the condition
# expression entirely, so `while (*(--tmp) == ' ')` yields no node --
# no `__deref`, no `__unary`, no `__binop.eq`. Only the body's
# `found.s--` survives, as a CollectionElement. A binding therefore has
# no node to label, and the construct this rank needs is unreachable
# from the data.
#
# The discriminant itself is loop-carried: which base the backwards
# step must stay above. Measured across every C/C++ checkout in the
# campaign's clone set (58 loop conditions dereferencing a
# pre-decremented pointer, after de-duplicating a project's
# vulnerable/fixed/HEAD copies), the *floorless* spelling is the
# majority idiom -- 49 of 58 -- and is safe by a contract the code
# cannot express: krb5's mkstemp `while(*--trv == 'X')` (the template
# is known to hold X's), libxml2's leading-zero strip
# `while(*(--ptr) == '0')` present at both revisions of its own rank,
# openssl's `while(*--p == '0')` and `while(max && *--rp == 0)`,
# zephyr's `while(*--buf == '0')`, utf8cpp's vendored `utf8::prior`
# `while(utf8::internal::is_trail(*(--it)))` in assimp and icinga2,
# ICU's `while(U8_IS_TRAIL(*--p))`, subversion's
# `while(svn_ctype_isspace(*--end))`, LibRaw's `while(*--cp == ' ')`
# and `while(isdigit(*--jext))`, upx's `while(0==*--uptr)`, klib's
# `while(*--search == string[i])`, hermes' `while(!*--xc)`, ceph's
# `while(*(--npath) != '/')` -- roughly 14 distinct projects firing per
# 1 true positive. Only 9 of 58 spell the floor, from 5 projects
# (asterisk, barebox, grpc's upb, vim, and the fixed opensips line
# itself). A shape-only rule is unshippable, and narrowing it onto this
# buffer's own spelling is a repro-shaped patch. The walk-base relation
# is the not-mechanical engine gap the ledger already carries for the
# family (1896 names this rank's sub-shape).
#
# No definition change shipped. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry beyond the
# native-parser bounds family already filed at 1896; this rank adds the
# root fact that C loop conditions are not lowered at all, which is the
# reason no node exists to hang a walk-bound fact on.
#
# ## Recheck measurements (knowledge base tip 11984e0e1)
#
# Baseline 3x3 over codecs.c: 20/20/20 vulnerable, 20/20/20 fixed,
# identical rule and line sets. `vyql match` on the vulnerable file
# lists no label at any line in 554-566. `vyql graph` on the minimal
# repro: no node for the loop condition. Clone-set sweep for loop
# conditions dereferencing a pre-decremented pointer: 58 hits, 49
# floorless from 14 projects, 9 floored from 5. Narrow spec passing
# with -v. Rank stays ATTENTION.

test "rank1528: the last-payload trim walks back with no floor"
  lang c
  file modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  code
  ```
  struct lump {
      union {
          char value[64];
      } u;
      int len;
  };

  struct str_field {
      char *s;
      int len;
  };

  int trim_last_payload(struct lump *lmp, struct str_field found, char *cur)
  {
      /* take the previous whitespaces as well */
      while (found.s > lmp->u.value && *(found.s - 1) == ' ') {
          found.s--;
          found.len++;
      }

      /* when trimming the very last payload, avoid trailing ws */
      if (cur == lmp->u.value + lmp->len) {
          char *tmp = found.s;
          while (*(--tmp) == ' ') {
              found.s--;
              found.len++;
          }
      }

      lmp->len -= found.len;
      return found.len;
  }
  ```

